/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * readConfig
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * readConfig(file)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) file (char *)   input configuration file
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Read the configuration file and set values
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Read configuration file line by line.  Look for a header which is
 * marked by surrounding square brackets, ie., [ motor 5], [mechanism slit],
 * and so on.  Valid headers are "motor", "mechanism", "filters",
 * "temperature", "cryo", and "grating".
 *
 * All the lines following this header and up to the next are parsed
 * by parseKeywordValue() except for "filters", which uses setFilters().
 *
 * Blank lines are ignored.  A '#' starts a comment, which continues until
 * the end of the line, and which is ignored.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * parseKeywordValue
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * parseKeywordValue(keyword, pItem, base, rhs, orig)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) keyword (char *)         keyword as determined by calling routine
 * (>) pItem (itemConfig *)     pointer to configuration description table
 * (>) base (char *)            pointer to storage area/structures for data
 * (>) rhs (char *)             right hand side of input (values)
 * (>) orig (char *)            original full input line, for error messages
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Determine and store value for given keyword
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Look up keyword in configuration description structure (pItem).  From
 * that, determine how to parse rest of line and where in the data
 * structure to store the value.  Convert the rhs and store, checking for
 * some errors.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * doPosition
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * doPosition(base, rhs, orig)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) base (char *)            pointer to storage area/structures for data
 * (>) rhs (char *)             right hand side of input (values)
 * (>) orig (char *)            original full input line, for error messages
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Parse and store configuration position information
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Allowed positions for a given mechanism are stored in linked list
 * data structures.  Parse the input line, which consists of name,
 * numeric position, and (optionally) index number.  Store the position
 * indexed by name in the appropriate linked list.  The index number,
 * a small positive integer, can be used as an alias for the named
 * position.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
